0;s:3:\"min\";i:1;s:3:\"max\";i:4000;s:4:\"step\";i:1;s:11:\"description\";s:110:\"Optional creative target from 1 to 4000 words. Leave blank to inherit the Connection and model recommendation.\";}s:16:\"prompt_max_words\";a:8:{s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"prompt_max_words\";s:4:\"type\";s:6:\"number\";s:5:\"label\";s:29:\"Maximum Prompt Length (words)\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:3:\"min\";i:1;s:3:\"max\";i:4000;s:4:\"step\";i:1;s:11:\"description\";s:130:\"Optional hard ceiling from 1 to 4000 words. It may tighten, but never loosen, a provider or model ceiling. Leave blank to inherit.\";}s:13:\"workflow_json\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:13:\"workflow_json\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:31:\"ComfyUI API Workflow (optional)\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:241:\"Paste a ComfyUI workflow exported with “Save (API Format)”. Managed Templates receive a published workflow automatically. A manually authored Template may leave this blank only when its checkpoint field defines a compatible simple graph.\";}s:20:\"provider_template_id\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:20:\"provider_template_id\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:37:\"Provider Template / Model Endpoint ID\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:283:\"Provider identifier paired with the Connection. For Suno or MidJourney use an api: or mcp: operation reference; for fal use a model endpoint ID; for ElevenLabs use a voice ID; for ComfyUI use the discovered MCP Template ID; for OpenRouter use a video model slug, e.g. google/veo-3.1.\";}s:18:\"configuration_json\";a:7:{s:4:\"name\";s:18:\"configuration_json\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:18:\"Configuration JSON\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:7:\"default\";s:2:\"{}\";s:11:\"description\";s:293:\"Optional provider-neutral JSON for parameter overrides, references, and SCF field mappings. The safe default is {}; managed Templates receive provider configuration automatically. Provider inputs live under {\"input\": {...}}; World Graph Studio adds the prompt and resolved bindings at runtime.\";}s:14:\"input_bindings\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:14:\"input_bindings\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:19:\"Input Bindings JSON\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:98:\"Optional JSON mapping prompt-related fields to Story Graph sources for the text-to-image workflow.\";}s:18:\"model_requirements\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:18:\"model_requirements\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:23:\"Model Requirements JSON\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:216:\"Optional JSON array of download sources for the models this Template loads: [{\"filename\":\"ltx-2.3.safetensors\",\"folder\":\"checkpoints\",\"url\":\"https://…\"}]. Used by the requirement check to offer a one-click install.\";}s:14:\"default_values\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:14:\"default_values\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:30:\"Default Values JSON (Advanced)\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:191:\"Advanced escape hatch for a flat JSON object of Template run-control defaults. Prefer the validated per-Template defaults editor in Generate Representative Media; it writes this field safely.\";}s:13:\"provider_type\";a:4:{s:4:\"name\";s:13:\"provider_type\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:13:\"Provider Type\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;}s:7:\"version\";a:4:{s:4:\"name\";s:7:\"version\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:7:\"Version\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;}s:6:\"status\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:6:\"status\";s:4:\"type\";s:6:\"select\";s:5:\"label\";s:6:\"Status\";s:8:\"required\";b:1;s:7:\"options\";a:3:{s:5:\"draft\";s:5:\"Draft\";s:6:\"active\";s:6:\"Active\";s:8:\"archived\";s:8:\"Archived\";}}}s:15:\"worldgraph_conn\";a:19:{s:15:\"connection_name\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:15:\"connection_name\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:15:\"Connection Name\";s:8:\"required\";b:1;s:11:\"description\";s:49:\"Human-readable name for this provider connection.\";}s:13:\"provider_type\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:13:\"provider_type\";s:4:\"type\";s:6:\"select\";s:5:\"label\";s:13:\"Provider Type\";s:8:\"required\";b:1;s:7:\"options\";a:17:{s:7:\"comfyui\";s:7:\"comfyui\";s:3:\"fal\";s:3:\"fal\";s:10:\"elevenlabs\";s:10:\"elevenlabs\";s:4:\"suno\";s:4:\"suno\";s:10:\"higgsfield\";s:10:\"higgsfield\";s:11:\"seedance_25\";s:11:\"seedance_25\";s:10:\"midjourney\";s:10:\"midjourney\";s:10:\"videodraft\";s:10:\"videodraft\";s:8:\"descript\";s:8:\"descript\";s:10:\"openrouter\";s:10:\"openrouter\";s:17:\"openai_compatible\";s:17:\"openai_compatible\";s:6:\"openai\";s:6:\"openai\";s:9:\"anthropic\";s:9:\"anthropic\";s:4:\"dual\";s:4:\"dual\";s:13:\"google_gemini\";s:13:\"google_gemini\";s:3:\"veo\";s:3:\"veo\";s:9:\"nova_reel\";s:9:\"nova_reel\";}s:11:\"description\";s:113:\"Provider adapter used by the paired Templates, such as ComfyUI, fal, Higgsfield, ElevenLabs, Suno, or MidJourney.\";}s:11:\"environment\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:11:\"environment\";s:4:\"type\";s:6:\"select\";s:5:\"label\";s:11:\"Environment\";s:8:\"required\";b:1;s:7:\"options\";a:4:{s:5:\"local\";s:5:\"Local\";s:11:\"development\";s:11:\"Development\";s:7:\"staging\";s:7:\"Staging\";s:10:\"production\";s:10:\"Production\";}}s:6:\"status\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:6:\"status\";s:4:\"type\";s:6:\"select\";s:5:\"label\";s:6:\"Status\";s:8:\"required\";b:1;s:7:\"options\";a:4:{s:10:\"unverified\";s:10:\"Unverified\";s:8:\"verified\";s:8:\"Verified\";s:5:\"error\";s:5:\"Error\";s:8:\"disabled\";s:8:\"Disabled\";}s:11:\"description\";s:98:\"Status is normally maintained by connection validation; set manually only to disable a connection.\";}s:10:\"is_default\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:10:\"is_default\";s:4:\"type\";s:6:\"select\";s:5:\"label\";s:17:\"Active Connection\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:7:\"options\";a:2:{s:2:\"no\";s:2:\"No\";s:3:\"yes\";s:3:\"Yes\";}s:11:\"description\";s:224:\"Marks this the active Connection Generate uses for its provider type and environment when a Template does not pin one. Only one Connection per provider type and environment can be active; setting this saves the others as No.\";}s:12:\"endpoint_url\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:12:\"endpoint_url\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:12:\"Endpoint URL\";s:8:\"required\";b:1;s:11:\"description\";s:264:\"Provider endpoint. For MidJourney REST use https://api.midjourney-api.com; for Higgsfield use https://platform.higgsfield.ai; for SunoAPI.org use https://api.sunoapi.org; for ElevenLabs use https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1; for local ComfyUI use its HTTP API base URL.\";}s:16:\"mcp_endpoint_url\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"mcp_endpoint_url\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:16:\"MCP Endpoint URL\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:254:\"Streamable HTTP MCP endpoint. Required for fal; use https://midjourney.mcp.acedata.cloud/mcp for MidJourney, https://mcp.higgsfield.ai/mcp for Higgsfield, or https://suno.mcp.acedata.cloud/mcp for Suno; optional for local ComfyUI discovery and downloads.\";}s:20:\"credential_reference\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:20:\"credential_reference\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:27:\"API Key / OAuth (Reference)\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:219:\"REST/API credential or environment reference, e.g. env://MIDJOURNEY_API_KEY, env://HIGGSFIELD_API_CREDENTIAL, env://SUNO_API_KEY, env://ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, or env://COMFYUI_API_KEY. Higgsfield expects KEY_ID:KEY_SECRET.\";}s:24:\"mcp_credential_reference\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:24:\"mcp_credential_reference\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:31:\"MCP API Key / OAuth (Reference)\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:228:\"Optional separate credential for the MCP endpoint. OAuth-enabled adapters manage this field through their Connect control; MidJourney and Suno MCP accept a service-scoped AceData Cloud token such as env://ACEDATACLOUD_API_TOKEN.\";}s:17:\"mcp_configuration\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:17:\"mcp_configuration\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:5:\"label\";s:24:\"MCP Configuration (JSON)\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:208:\"Optional non-secret MCP deployment settings as a JSON object, such as transport, host, port, path, Docker service, or startup health-check details. Keep credentials in the MCP API Key / OAuth reference field.\";}s:12:\"capabilities\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:12:\"capabilities\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:5:\"label\";s:19:\"Capabilities (JSON)\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:179:\"Optional non-secret capability profile. Use chat, vision, asset_generation, and modalities to describe what this Connection and model can do; pair asset modalities with Templates.\";}s:5:\"model\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:5:\"model\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:5:\"Model\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:146:\"Optional default model. For SunoAPI.org use V5_5 (mapped to chirp-v5-5 for MCP); for fal use an endpoint ID; for ElevenLabs use a speech model ID.\";}s:10:\"max_tokens\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:10:\"max_tokens\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:10:\"Max Tokens\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:33:\"Maximum tokens for LLM responses.\";}s:11:\"temperature\";a:5:{s:4:\"name\";s:11:\"temperature\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:5:\"label\";s:11:\"Temperature\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:55:\"Creativity level (0.0 = deterministic, 1.0 = creative).\";}s:12:\"model_access\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:12:\"model_access\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:12:\"Model Access\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:221:\"Optional JSON allowlist. MidJourney and Higgsfield use reviewed transport-operation references; fal uses model endpoint IDs; ElevenLabs uses voice IDs; Suno uses model version IDs. Empty lets the adapter select a default.\";}s:18:\"enabled_structures\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:18:\"enabled_structures\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:18:\"Enabled Structures\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:104:\"JSON array of generation structures enabled for this connection, e.g. [\"character-sheet\",\"scene-image\"].\";}s:17:\"enabled_templates\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:17:\"enabled_templates\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:30:\"Added Workflows (Managed JSON)\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:158:\"Internal links between provider workflows added through Workflow Setup and their reusable Generation Templates. Managed automatically; edit only for recovery.\";}s:11:\"rate_limits\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:11:\"rate_limits\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:11:\"Rate Limits\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:64:\"JSON object, e.g. {\"max_concurrent\":1,\"requests_per_minute\":10}.\";}s:13:\"cost_controls\";a:6:{s:4:\"name\";s:13:\"cost_controls\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"textarea\";s:6:\"format\";s:4:\"json\";s:5:\"label\";s:13:\"Cost Controls\";s:8:\"required\";b:0;s:11:\"description\";s:63:\"JSON object, e.g. {\"max_cost_per_job\":0.5,\"monthly_budget\":50}.\";}}}', 'auto'),
